        <item>
            <title>1.3.2</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 17:10:34 +0300</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>8</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<!-- What Sparkle shows for 1.3.2. generate_appcast embeds any
     Belay-<version>.html beside the matching DMG, and publish-appcast.sh
     copies it there. One file per version, English only: Sparkle does not
     negotiate locale, and plain English is better than half-localised notes. -->
<style>
  body { font: 13px -apple-system, sans-serif; color: #333; margin: 12px 16px; }
  h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 6px 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  p.quiet { color: #777; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #ddd; } p.quiet { color: #999; }
  }
</style>
<h2>Belay 1.3.2</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Codex gets precise detection.</b> Belay now reads Codex&#8217;s own
      turn markers, so starts and finishes are exact and retries get the same
      patience as Claude Code. No setup needed.</li>
  <li><b>Two more agents are built in.</b> Copilot CLI and OpenCode now have
      ready-made presets. One click to add either one.</li>
  <li><b>Background work still counts.</b> If a turn ends while background
      agents or shell jobs are still running, Belay keeps the Mac awake until
      they finish.</li>
  <li><b>The network stays awake too.</b> While Belay is holding, it also asks
      macOS to keep the network active, so SSH sessions and streaming replies
      can keep going.</li>
</ul>
<p class="quiet">Also: Belay knows you&#8217;re needed as soon as an agent asks
a question, and presets now say clearly when their folder is missing.</p>]]></description>
