            <description><![CDATA[<!-- What Sparkle shows for 1.3.1. generate_appcast embeds any
     Belay-<version>.html beside the matching DMG, and publish-appcast.sh
     copies it there. One file per version, English only: Sparkle does not
     negotiate locale, and plain English is better than half-localised notes. -->
<style>
  body { font: 13px -apple-system, sans-serif; color: #333; margin: 12px 16px; }
  h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 6px 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  p.quiet { color: #777; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #ddd; } p.quiet { color: #999; }
  }
</style>
<h2>Belay 1.3.1</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>The chart follows your cursor.</b> Hover over a day in Statistics and
      the numbers switch to that day. Move away and the totals come back.</li>
  <li><b>Pi is built in.</b> One click adds Pi with the same local session
      watching that already worked through manual setup. Asked for on GitHub.</li>
  <li><b>Quiet sessions stay quiet.</b> If an agent stops mid-answer, Belay now
      says it went quiet instead of calling the run finished.</li>
  <li><b>Closed-lid stops explain themselves.</b> If the time limit or heat
      protection ends a closed-lid hold, the notification tells you why.</li>
</ul>
<p class="quiet">Also: the helper status updates as soon as you approve it,
and failed update checks now say why in the log.</p>]]></description>
